<!-- =====================================================
     ESOURCE AI GROUP — PRESENTER PAGE (/presenter-aig/)  v3.1
     Presentation player on the Bill Evans presenter agent.
     Reads ?course=N; list from esource-aig-course-files/presentations.json
     v3.3: LANGUAGE GATE.
     - A centered chooser over a grayed-out screen appears before
       the welcome video. One choice sets: Bill's greeting, Bill's
       spoken language, the slide translations, AND the welcome
       video's subtitles (Vimeo texttrack), then plays the video.
     - Subtitles only appear for languages already generated on the
       video in Vimeo (one-time job per video).
     Carried from v3.2: self-healing flow, voice-timed slide turns,
     live transcript with duplicate filtering.
     v4.0: EVENT-DRIVEN slide turns — deadlock-proof owed-turn queue.
     v4.1: the end-of-voice event must HOLD 1.2s (audio-chunk blips
     cancel it); the self-healer only sends [CONTINUE] and never turns
     pages itself — one advance_slide call = exactly one turn.
     v5.0: CONFIRMED FLOW — same mechanism as the teacher pages. Bill
     asks, the listener confirms (any language), advance_slide turns the
     screen INSTANTLY, and Bill presents the slide the tool reply names.
     No queue, no settle timers. Slide-1 guard: early advance calls are
     ignored for the first 8 seconds. Pause = simply not confirming
     (plus the prompt's pause rule); hand-raise unchanged.
     v5.2: the greeting itself ends with "Are you ready to begin?" —
     no [BEGIN PRESENTATION] signal, no waiting; the listener's answer
     starts the deck. (Greeting text lives in presentations.json.)
     v5.3: slide-1 guard is state-based — while on slide 1, advance_slide
     is refused until Bill has spoken twice (greeting + slide-1 delivery),
     so the first "yes" can never skip slide 1.
     v5.4: Pause/Resume button — pauses WITHOUT ending the session (Bill's
     audio to zero + mic muted + stay-silent note); Resume restores both
     and Bill continues on the same slide with his memory intact.
     Requires the v2.0 prompt (PRESENTING — CONFIRMED FLOW).
     v5.5: sends course_number (the ?course=N value) so the agent's
     COURSE SWITCH loads only this presentation's files.
     v5.6: slide updates say "viewer" (not "learner").
     v5.7: raised-hand and Pause/Resume buttons removed (the viewer
     simply starts speaking to ask a question).
     ===================================================== -->
<style>
